# Life Admin — UI/UX Design Specification

## 1. Design Direction

Create a clean, modern productivity application.

Design goals:
- Simple.
- Professional.
- Calm.
- Information-dense without feeling crowded.
- Mobile-first.
- Accessible.
- Fast to scan.

Avoid:
- Excessive gradients.
- Decorative animations.
- Overloaded dashboards.
- Large blocks of unnecessary text.
- Color-only status indicators.

## 2. Application Shell

Desktop:
- Left sidebar.
- Main content area.
- User/profile menu.

Mobile:
- Compact top header.
- Collapsible navigation.
- Full-width content.

Primary navigation:
- Dashboard
- Documents
- Settings (if implemented)

## 3. Dashboard Layout

Header:
- Page title.
- Short supporting description.
- Add Document button.

Stats:
- Total Documents.
- Expiring Soon.
- Expired.

Renewals:
- Upcoming renewal list.
- Expiry date.
- Status.
- Link to all documents.

Quick actions:
- Add Document.
- View Documents.

## 4. Dashboard Wireframe

Dashboard

[ Dashboard title ]                         [ + Add Document ]

[ Total Documents ] [ Expiring Soon ] [ Expired ]

[ Quick Actions ]

Upcoming Renewals                                  [ View all ]

[ Document ] [ Category ] [ Expiry ] [ Status ]

## 5. Documents Page

Header:
- Documents title.
- Description.
- Add Document button.

Toolbar:
- Search.
- Category filter.
- Status filter.
- Sort control.

List:
Desktop:
- Table.

Mobile:
- Cards.

## 6. Document Table Columns

- Document.
- Category.
- Document Number where available.
- Expiry Date.
- Status.
- Actions.

## 7. Document Card

Each card should show:
- Title.
- Category.
- Document number if available.
- Expiry date.
- Status badge.
- View/Edit/Delete actions.

## 8. Status Design

ACTIVE:
- Text: `Active`

EXPIRING_SOON:
- Text: `Expiring Soon`

EXPIRED:
- Text: `Expired`

NO_EXPIRY:
- Text: `No Expiry`

Status must include text plus visual distinction.

## 9. Color Semantics

Use restrained semantic colors:
- Neutral for normal UI.
- Green family for Active.
- Amber/yellow family for Expiring Soon.
- Red family for Expired.
- Gray family for No Expiry.

Do not hard-code meaning into color alone.

## 10. Typography

Suggested hierarchy:
- Page title: large, bold.
- Section heading: medium/semibold.
- Card value: large/bold.
- Body: readable 14–16px.
- Supporting text: smaller/muted.

## 11. Responsive Breakpoints

Mobile first.

Use:
- Base styles for mobile.
- `sm:` for small/tablet layouts.
- `md:` for medium layouts.
- `lg:` for desktop layouts.

Example:
- Stats: 1 column mobile, 2 tablet, 3 desktop.
- Documents: cards mobile, table desktop.

## 12. Forms

Document form fields:
- Title.
- Category.
- Document Number.
- Issue Date.
- Expiry Date.
- Notes.

Use:
- Visible labels.
- Helpful placeholders.
- Inline validation.
- Required indicators.
- Save/cancel actions.
- Disabled loading state.

## 13. Empty State

No documents:

No documents yet

Add your first document to start tracking important expiry dates.

[ + Add Document ]

## 14. Error State

Unable to load documents.

Something went wrong. Please try again.

[ Try Again ]

## 15. Delete Confirmation

Title:
`Delete Document?`

Message:
`Are you sure you want to delete "Document Name"? This action cannot be undone.`

Actions:
- Cancel
- Delete

## 16. Accessibility

- Semantic HTML.
- Keyboard accessible controls.
- Visible focus states.
- Proper labels.
- Sufficient contrast.
- Do not rely solely on color.
- Buttons must describe their action.
- Dialogs must trap/focus correctly where a dialog component is used.

## 17. Tailwind Component Style

Common patterns:
- Cards: `rounded-xl border bg-white shadow-sm`
- Buttons: consistent padding, radius, font weight.
- Inputs: border, focus ring, readable height.
- Badges: compact pill with text.
- Layout: `space-y-*`, `gap-*`, responsive grid utilities.

The exact visual style may evolve, but consistency is required.
